From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mem: one SqEntryCell module per physical store-queue entry

PhysicalStoreQueue unrolls its per-entry logic over StoreQueuePhysicalSize
entries -- sta stage 1 and 2 allocation, std data valid, cancel and
dequeue, handle-finish -- and writes the entries by index from the store
pipelines and the commit logic. As one module of 22 k lines it was the
longest synthesis partition of the core: 56 minutes, 36 of them in abc.

SqEntryCell holds one entry's data and control registers and every write
to them, in the order the queue made them; the entry index is an input,
so all instances are one module and synthesis maps it once. The queue
keeps dataEntries, ctrlEntries and needCancel as read views of the
cells; ForwardModule, DeqModule and everything else that reads them is
unchanged. Behaviour is unchanged.

Carried by the bazel-orfs CoreMark/Joule study; not upstreamed.
---
